ames>GD</given-names></name><name><surname>Hogue</surname><given-names>CWV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Analyzing yeast protein-protein interaction data obtained from different sources</article-title><source><italic>Nature Biotechnology</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>20</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>991</fpage><lpage>997</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12355115</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>von Mering</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Krause</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Snel</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Comparative assessment of large-scale data sets of protein-protein interactions</article-title><source><italic>Nature</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>417</volume><issue>6887</issue><fpage>399</fpage><lpage>403</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12000970</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hakes</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Robertson</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Oliver</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of dataset selection on the topological interpretation of protein interaction networks</article-title><source><italic>BMC Genomics</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>131</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16174296</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henrick</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Thornton</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>PQS: a protein quaternary structure file server</article-title><s